# armour/shared/pauldron_scale3_r: the medium scale pauldron on the right shoulder (scale.3; LADDER-ARMOUR,
# STYLE_P2 25.6 / 27.4: mail, scale and lamellar shoulders): rows of scale units on a cop, 2 px past the shoulder line,
# a solid band rim; the near views lit at the top-left, the far one in shadow behind the arm. It rides the lean and
# the bob and lifts a pixel on wind-ups (`up`). Finish regions: R the rim band, P the cop's face, W a spot on the shadow side.
# Shared by both bodies (D10). Format: rpg/art/doll/doll.h. Source: LADDER-ARMOUR's pauld.py + expand.py (fill: scale).
# (LADDER-ARMOUR alloys i1) a step-4 specular on the lit top of the first scales / lames / plates (top-left light):
# with no step 4 a coloured alloy read as clay; the glint and the dark core make any metal read as metal.
# (FORGE-MANTLE, envelope R3) the base D / U views one column wider on the outer side (tools: widen.py, base views only): size 3
# reaches 2 px past the 16 px line, 20 px across (PLAN T3, the fair test's guard); the forge `shoulder-scale` views unchanged.
use person
role pauldron scale.3
layer armNear
anchor shoulderR
keys pauld
z 5
side R
# (FORGE-MANTLE, round 2) `when shoulder-scale replace` views: the DROP mass drawn for the forge styles (STYLE_P2 28.3; generated by FORGE-MANTLE gen.py from shapes5.py); 0-forge looks keep the base views.

